        "body": "`requireContentType()` accepted malformed values such as `application/json/extra`, `application/json junk`, and `application/(json)` when a wildcard matched. Exact accepted types sent these malformed values to the 415 branch instead of the documented 422 branch.\n\nValidate the complete type/subtype as HTTP tokens before matching accepted types, following [RFC 9110 sections 8.3.1 and 5.6.2](https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9110.html#name-media-type). Existing wildcard matching, parameter handling, case normalization, and valid token punctuation are preserved. No API or dependency changes.\n\nFixes #1633.\n\nValidation with Node 24:\n\n- New matrix cases: 36 failures on main across web/Node and exact/subtype/full wildcards; eight valid-token controls pass before and after. All 82 query tests pass with the fix.\n- `pnpm test`: lint, TypeScript, and all 73 test files pass; **3,174 tests passed, 51 skipped**, with no type errors. Statement coverage: 96.25%.\n- `pnpm build` passes. Built Node and generic entry points return 422 for the malformed examples and 200 for a valid type.\n\nThis contribution is AI-assisted.\n\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated comment: release notes by coderabbit.ai -->\n\n<!-- coderabbit-ai-generated:v1 -->\n\n## Summary by CodeRabbit\n\n* **Bug Fixes**\n  * Requests with malformed content types are now rejected with a 422 response, including values with missing type or subtype, invalid token characters, or extra slashes.\n  * Valid content types continue to be accepted, including uppercase values, parameters, structured suffixes, and digit-leading types. Accepted values are normalized for matching.\n\n<!-- end of auto-generated comment: release notes by coderabbit.ai -->",
